      "message": "I wasn\u0027t even aware of that. Thanks for the pointer.\n\nI added BOARD_OPTION because I wasn\u0027t sure if weak functions are accepted in Chrome EC, they\u0027re sometimes used, but often stuff is hidden behind ifdefs like here. We need some way to keep the old behavior (\"kblight support compiled in \u003d\u003e kblight exists\") as the default. BOARD_OPTION provides that.\nI\u0027d rather go with a weak default implementation and always run through the if (board_has_kblight()) part. Is that okay?\n\nMore generally, I think EC_FEATURE_PWM_KEYB needs to be adapted to the new situation. That should be safe as long as the default mirrors the old behavior (ie defaults to 1 unless the board states otherwise).\n\nAfter that, I guess we could expose EC_FEATURES in EC_ACPI_MEM, but that\u0027ll need 4 addresses (for the 32 feature flags), and another bit to determine if features are readable (since we can\u0027t differentiate 8 \"1\" features from the 0xff default). Those 5 bytes will be at a different offset since \n\nI\u0027ll work on that.",
